{\b English}\par
{\b License: EUPL-1.2}\par
European Union Public Licence. Full text: https://eupl.eu/1.2/en/ and in the repository https://github.com/cryptobones-1337/deR4Tizer\par
The software is provided "as is", without warranty. It is a proof of concept, not audited. The binaries are not signed yet: Windows shows "unknown publisher".\par
\par
{\b What the installation does}\par
\'b7 The deR4Tizer service (SYSTEM account, automatic start) monitors connections, persistence and the local network, and raises alerts.\par
\'b7 It turns on Windows security logging (local group policy).\par
\'b7 It places hidden decoy files in Documents, Pictures and the Desktop, to spot ransomware.\par
\'b7 Two automatic responses are on by default, adjustable in the interface: firewall block of Spamhaus DROP and Feodo Tracker addresses (lifted after 7 days), and suspension of a program that touches the decoy files (never resumed automatically).\par
\'b7 The interface starts on its own under the account of each signed-in user, without administrator rights (scheduled task and sign-in), unless the LANCEMENT_SESSION=0 option is used. The installer does not start it.\par
\'b7 Downloads: threat lists, JA3 fingerprints, GeoIP database, LOLDrivers list, and a daily version check. No update is installed automatically by default.\par
\'b7 No data from this computer is sent to a third party, except the alerts you choose to forward (ntfy, Teams, e-mail, syslog); the downloads contact the servers that publish these lists and versions.\par
\'b7 deR4Tizer works alongside Microsoft Defender: it neither turns it off nor weakens it, and does not replace it. The baseline, if you apply it, can strengthen some of its settings.\par
\'b7 Uninstalling removes the blocks, the task and the settings it set. Options: GARDER_DONNEES=1 keeps the data, GARDER_BASELINE=1 keeps the applied baseline.\par
Lists used by default: Spamhaus DROP, abuse.ch Feodo Tracker and SSLBL. Map: Natural Earth (public domain).\par
